# PY046: --data-size makes compared workloads unequal and run-order-dependent
#
# CONFIRMED — static analysis (benchmark correctness)
#
# With --data-size, number_name() (speedtest.py:131-135) consumes global random
# state via random.randint(). Bindings SQL invokes it during execution while
# no-bindings SQL invokes it during generation. Reused binding workloads
# generate different data across drivers and iterations from mutable seeded
# state. Alternating driver order changes which driver consumes each portion.
